  "changes": [
    "The existing cohort variation panel can pin one displayed cohort as reference A while the learner browses cohort B on another island or recorded generation.",
    "The reference captures its island, generation, species, resident count, raw trait mean and five trait-band counts. Reference evidence stays attached to its original cohort.",
    "Paired bars compare each cohort using its own resident total, including six-founder and 24-resident cohorts. Native band buttons continue to inspect actual members of displayed cohort B.",
    "A details table shows exact resident counts and ratios, rounded shares and B-minus-A share differences. The mean difference uses trait index points; share differences use percentage points.",
    "Same-cohort and cross-species states explain why there is no comparative distribution. Empty cohorts have explicit undefined means, shares and dependent differences.",
    "Visiting the reference navigates its recorded generation, island and species, clears organism selection and focuses the variation heading. Clearing the reference returns focus to the persistent heading.",
    "The reference is local presentation state guarded by founding-frame identity; it is cleared when the world is replaced, including replacement with the same seed."
  ],
  "scientificCorrectness": [
    "The same species and inherited trait are required for a numerical comparison. Equal summary statistics do not make different island or generation cohorts identical.",
    "Five fixed bands use raw means: [0,.2), [.2,.4), [.4,.6), [.6,.8), and [.8,1]. Counts retain all residents and the last band includes the upper endpoint.",
    "A and B proportions use their own whole-cohort denominators. An empty cohort does not imply a zero mean or zero share; comparisons requiring those values are undefined.",
    "Geographic, temporal and combined context differences are explicitly distinguished. A geographic contrast is not proof of separate species; temporal contrasts do not depict changes within an individual.",
    "This descriptive comparison does not isolate selection, dispersal, drift or mutation. Trait spread does not measure genome-wide genetic diversity or rank breeding success.",
    "Only presentation state and existing navigation change. The evolutionary model, world history and RNG are unchanged."
  ],
